nn7le05ob02re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "In Karel Capek's play, <span class=\"italic\">R.U.R.</span>, robots were featured for the first time. The mechanical workers were created by a wealthy industrialist who had them run his factory. They revolted and took it over. After this, robots began to appear in films, novels, and on TV. Many were benevolent. Some were not.", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn7le05ob02re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "In 1950, Isaac Asimov posed questions in <span class=\"italic\">I, Robot</span>. What if there came a time when robots were just like people?  What would the world be like if robots enjoyed the same rights that humans enjoy? What laws would govern them?", "id": 2, "time": "22000", "image": "engenn7le05ob02re2img03.jpg"}, {"text": "These questions prompted others. As we ventured into the future, how would robots integrate into our lives? <span class=\"italic\">Lost in Space</span> and <span class=\"italic\">Forbidden Planet</span> showed oversized robots as part of exploration teams. In <span class=\"italic\">The Jetsons</span> robot Rosie, who rolled around on castors, cared for the family.", "id": 3, "time": "38000", "image": "engenn7le05ob02re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "<p><span class=\"italic\">Star Wars</span> featured protocol translator C-3PO and his long-time counterpart, R2-D2. Then came <span class=\"italic\">WALL-E</span>, the robotic unit which scientists designed to clean up a waste-covered Earth, who fell in love.</p>What famous robot do you wish you could invite into your life?", "id": 4, "time": "58000", "image": "engenn7le05ob02re2img01.jpg"}], "audiosrc": "engenn7le05ob02re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn7le05ob02re2img02.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "_data": [], "type": "audio", "template_override": 1}, {"id": 2, "title": "", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [], "audiosrc": "engenn7le05ob02re6aud01", "coverimg": "engenn7le05ob02re6img01.jpg"}, "type": "picture"}], "_data": [], "type": "audio", "template_override": 1}]}]}